      "message": "test(sim): the new-block-after-flip pin judges blocks that differ from above\n\nThe pin compared the program verdict (top - part per column) of the\ncarried run against the new-block run. Both starting stocks stood 60 x 60\nwith a Z18 top and differed only below the part, and Face2 faced both to\nthe part top, so both verdicts were exactly zero by construction. The\ntest failed on #408's own branch head as well; neither #410 nor the merge\ncaused it, and the sim's Entry::NewBlock path is correct.\n\nThe fixture now gives Setup2 its own 24 mm block (top Z22) and stops\nFace2 at Z19. The carried run reads 2 mm of rest and the new block 3 mm.\nBoth values are pinned, along with the verdict difference and the\nundo/redo round trip.\n\nFixes #415\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
